// The silent half of consumer KB-21: two METHOD bodies under one name compiled with no message at all,
// and the last one answered every call — this program built and returned 222. A careless merge or a
// rebase that lands one function twice replaced a method's behaviour and nothing said so. kama has no
// overloading, so a member name is declared once, like a file-scope function.
type value Box {
    isize count;
    public ctor make() { this.count = 1; }
    public const fn isize get() { return 111; }
    public const fn isize get() { return 222; }   // ERROR: duplicate method
}
fn int32 main() { Box b = Box.make(); return cast<int32>(b.get()); }
